00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:08.070 align:start position:0%
dozens of ecuadorians gathered outside  this prison on saturday waiting for any  news of their family members  there was an overnight riot at the  littoral penitentiary in the southern  city of guayaquil that began on friday  evening  information is difficult to come by  they desperately looked through an  unofficial list of victims names that  was posted outside the building  i'm hoping that my son is one of the  injured but we don't know anything  because there's no official list from  the authorities only lista has been  leaked but we don't know anything  nothing is known what the prisoners are  saying from inside is that no police or  military are controlling it that they  are letting them kill each other in cold  blood  police are blaming rival gangs for the  violence  these events are due to a territory  dispute by criminal gangs inside the  prison at the moment there are certain  pavilions that are without leaders  because this may be surprising to all  citizens but the leaders were released  after having served 60 of their sentence  at the same prison earlier this year  more than 100 inmates were killed in the  worst incident of prison violence in  recent years  ecuador's prison system has come under  the spotlight recently for overcrowding  and poor sanitation and living  conditions  officials say they are accommodating  about 9 000 more inmates than the  prisons were designed for  the literal penitentiary was built for 5  300 inmates but it holds  500.  in september president guillermo lasso  declared a two-month state of emergency  in the prison system  he's also called on the highest court to  allow the military to enter prisons to  stop any violence  the court responded in a statement  ecuador's prison crisis will require  more than temporary solutions  dorsa japari al jazeera
 

